{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/841276-capturing-werewolves","id":841276,"title":"Capturing werewolves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-03T06:56:54-08:00","id":841276,"title":"Capturing werewolves","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> I'm playing the adventure Rite of Passage and my characters are about to attack the mine*. According to the story if they do so they should be captured. But I'm afraid if combat starts it's more likely they get killed than captured.<br /> <br /> *in short the mine is a strip mine that smells like wyrm and looks only protected by a few fomori. But then there is a pack of rank 3-4 black spiral dancers and some Tremere antitribu. The PC are still rank 0 (that's why the adventure is called Rite of Passage)<br /> <br /> Do you have any suggestion on how to present the scene with a low risk of killing the characters without looking &quot;the NPC are doing stupid stuff because the ST don't want to kill us&quot;?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T08:45:29-08:00","id":841327,"title":"","content":"I haven't read Rite of Passage, but it stands to reason to me that the BSDs might *want* to capture the PCs. So I don't think they have to do stupid things, just act with that goal in mind. From the BSDs perspective I see baby werewolves ripe for the corrupting or interrogating or breeding or just for the lols of being evil. If the BSDs make a point to do bashing then when the PC falls unconscious they should revert to breed form, which won't heal every turn and would therefore stay knocked out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8365-pensman","name":"Pensman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8365_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T08:46:42-08:00","id":841328,"title":"","content":"The players are mere puppies hurling themselves at the Wyrm's Chosen. The Black Spiral Dancers would likely be both willing and able to overpower the weaker, inexperienced Garou- and once the pack has been tortured and humiliated, or perhaps even willingly won over, they will be cast down into Malfeas to walk the Black Spiral.<br /> <br /> Black Spiral Dancers are brutal, violent monsters, but they are also happy to pervert and taint loyal Garou. The PC's pack sound like ideal targets: pups fresh from their first change, who may not be fully indoctrinated against serving the glorious Wyrm...<br /> <br /> Edit: curses, beaten to the punch by one minute. I will add that the bashing damage idea is great... removing limbs is also an option for dealing with uppity Gaians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 03-03-2016, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T11:23:22-08:00","id":841400,"title":"","content":"It's also worth noting that while Garou have impressive immune systems, they aren't that strong against magical toxins; hence the effects of the Resist Toxin Gift.<br /> <br /> If the PCs are cubs, without Gifts, then it is painfully simple for a pack of more experienced BSD to use mystically awakened paralytics on them. It's not a great tactic against default Rank 1 Garou (since Resist Toxin is pretty common), but it makes capturing cubs much easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T11:29:07-08:00","id":841403,"title":"","content":"Let the players scout out the situation first, be aware of how many enemies they are up against and see if any of them come up with a plan to take them out/have enemy fight each other/ use the mine to their advantage and see where it goes.<br /> <br /> I'd rather that as a player and an ST than completely rail road what absolutely must happen and will happen how. Give them the chance and the choice, should the fall they fell fighting and perhaps with a win or two before being over powered and awaking as prisoners. If that's what happens.<br /> <br /> That's what I'd do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T01:00:58-08:00","id":841773,"title":"","content":"To capture a garou, you might want to not use agg damage or have enemies switch to bashing, once they have cause some wounds. Unlike vampires, garou don't halve the bashing damage, iirc, but may remove one bashing each round, without a roll (lethal with a roll). So clubs or other blunt weapons or certain maneuvers will render the characters unconscious. Also, if one is helpless in that way, the bad guess could threaten to deliver a death blow, if the rest doesn't surrender.<br /> <br /> Poison that renders the players helpless might also be an option, although I don't remember specific rules.<br /> <br /> Shackles made of silver are describes as a torture device (since it makes garou feel uneasy) and will destroy Gnosis points. Also, strong shackles won't bend or rip apart like un-dedicated clothing and therefore break the garous bones and joints if they shift out of homid, rendering them helpless. A collar might choke them until they loose consciousness and revert to breed form.<br /> <br /> Revised introduced a Rite that severs a room from the penumbra, specifically to create prisons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:54:29-08:00","id":842294,"title":"","content":"DNA uses a capture grenade it stands to reason that such devices could make it onto the black market.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}